Tests vNIC DLPAR add/remove operations spanning two LPARs (LPAR1 = local
machine running the test, LPAR2 = a remote LPAR accessed over SSH) that
share the same physical SR-IOV adapter.

Two test methods are provided:

  test_multi_lpar_same_adapter
      Add a vNIC backed by adapter A (same physical port) to both LPAR1 and
      LPAR2.  Ping from each LPAR to the peer to verify simultaneous network
      connectivity.  Remove both vNICs at the end.
      YAML: vnic_multi_lpar_same_adapter.yaml

  test_multi_lpar_different_ports
      Add a vNIC backed by adapter A port 0 to LPAR1 and adapter A port 1
      to LPAR2.  Both share the same physical card but use different physical
      ports.  Ping from each LPAR to the peer.  Remove both vNICs at the end.
      YAML: vnic_multi_lpar_different_ports.yaml
How to run
----------
# Test 1 - same adapter, same port
avocado run vnic_multi_lpar.py:VnicMultiLpar.test_multi_lpar_same_adapter \
          -m vnic_multi_lpar.py.data/vnic_multi_lpar_same_adapter.yaml \
          --max-parallel-tasks=1

# Test 2 - same adapter, different ports
avocado run vnic_multi_lpar.py:VnicMultiLpar.test_multi_lpar_different_ports \
          -m vnic_multi_lpar.py.data/vnic_multi_lpar_different_ports.yaml \
          --max-parallel-tasks=1
Notes:
--------
- The cleanup phase (vNIC remove from both LPARs) runs unconditionally in a
  try/finally block, so no interfaces are left stranded even when an
  earlier phase fails.

- If the test fails mid-run and is re-executed, any leftover IP address on
  LPAR1's interface is silently flushed before re-adding, preventing the
  "Address already assigned" error on re-runs.
